        rules: {
          objective: "Beat the dealer's 5-card poker hand. Dealer must qualify (hold A-K or better) for the Raise bet to pay.",
          gameplay: 'Ante. Deal 5 each (dealer 1 up). Player may fold (lose ante) or Raise (2× ante). Dealer reveals. Dealer must qualify (A-K or better). If qualified, compare hands; player wins 1:1 on ante, paytable on Raise. If not qualified, ante refunded, Raise push.',
          keyRules: [
            'No drawing â€” hands are played as dealt (5-card stud).',
            'Players may NOT discuss hands with each other (house rules).',
            'Dealer must qualify (A-K or better) for Raise bet to be in play.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Always raise with a pair or better. Always fold with less than A-K. With A-K hand, raise if dealer's face-up card is A or K and you hold another A or K in hand.",
          intermediate: "Optimal strategy: Raise with pair or better always. Fold with less than A-K. With A-K high: raise if dealer's up-card matches any of your other 4 cards.",
          advanced: 'House edge cannot be eliminated. The progressive jackpot side bet has very poor EV unless jackpot is extremely high (~$200,000+ for break-even on $1 bet with royal flush). Basic strategy reduces house edge from ~5.7% to ~5.2%.',
          tips: [
            'Never make the progressive jackpot side bet unless the jackpot is above ~$200,000.',
            'Dealer qualifying rule means folding preserves 1 Ante unit vs risking 3 total units.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
